HTTPUpgrade server: a read deadline and a size limit on the upgrade request, and keep accepting

Upstream: c320e89108c73b3d83ace6c2f32db1da7a48e5d4

At the pin, upgrade() reads the request with http.ReadRequest on the raw connection with no
deadline and no size limit, and keepAccepting returns on the first Accept error, after which the
inbound accepts nothing until the core restarts. Upstream #6463 (first in v26.7.11) gives the read
4 seconds, the WebSocket hub's ReadHeaderTimeout, and 12288 bytes, the read limit net/http derives
from that hub's MaxHeaderBytes of 8192, and keeps accepting after transient errors as the RAW hub
does.
The changes in transport/internet/httpupgrade/hub.go are upstream's, without its comment line;
only the hunk context differs, because xray-trusted-xff.patch, applied before this patch, changes
the same file further down. transport/internet/httpupgrade/handshake_deadline_test.go is fork code:
a request that stops before its blank line is closed after about 4 seconds, a valid upgrade
request with 16 KiB of headers is refused and one with 8 KiB is still upgraded.

